# Data Analytics Practical File

## Course Details

- **Course Name:** Data Analytics
- **Course Code:** CSE2500
- **Semester:** 5th Semester
- **Academic Year:** 2026–2027
- **Branch:** Computer Science Engineering
- **University:** Presidency University

## About This Repository

This repository contains my Data Analytics practical file, which demonstrates the evaluation of a machine learning classification model using a confusion matrix and various performance metrics.

The practical includes numerical calculations, Python programming, data preprocessing, model training, evaluation, and graphical representations.

## Practical: Confusion Matrix and Evaluation Metrics

### Part A: Numerical Analysis

A disease-prediction model is evaluated using 200 patients.

The confusion matrix values are:

- True Positive (TP): 70
- True Negative (TN): 100
- False Positive (FP): 20
- False Negative (FN): 10

The evaluation metrics obtained are:

| Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Accuracy | 85.00% |
| Precision | 77.78% |
| Recall | 87.50% |
| F1-Score | 82.35% |

### Part B: Real Dataset Workflow

The practical also demonstrates a machine learning workflow using the Breast Cancer Wisconsin dataset.

The workflow includes:

1. Data preprocessing
2. Checking missing values and duplicate rows
3. Splitting the dataset into training and testing sets
4. Feature standardization using StandardScaler
5. Training a Logistic Regression model
6. Evaluating the model using performance metrics
7. Visualizing the results

### Tools and Technologies

- Python
- Google Colab
- NumPy
- Pandas
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Scikit-learn
- GitHub

## Conclusion

This practical helped demonstrate how confusion matrices and evaluation metrics are used to measure the performance of classification models. It also provided an understanding of the machine learning workflow, including preprocessing, training, testing, and visualization.

